(A list declared in one branch inside a function, under the name of a
 top-level buffer, lasts as long as the branch. After it, the name is the
 top-level buffer again, on the call that took the branch and on the one
 that did not.)
a buffer called hold is "abc".

To 'branchy' with a number called n.
    If n is 1 then,
        a list called hold is [1, 2],
        Print "in branch {hold}".
    For each k from 1 to 2000, append "QQQQQQQQ" to hold.
    Print "after branch size {hold's size}".

'branchy' of 1.
a list called other is [5, 6, 7].
Print "other {other}".
'branchy' of 2.
Print "top {hold's size}".
Print "other {other}".
